      sqrt(2t)/sqrt(1/4+t^2) = 0.3759237506 (t=t1).  Rigorous EM upper bound at N=1e5: 0.37600351.
      CORRECT STATEMENT: |S_N(1/2+it)-zeta(1/2+it)| = sqrt(N)/|s-1| + O(N^{-1/2}),
      so at a zero S_N itself is ~ sqrt(N)/|s-1| and the zero appears only after cancellation.
  C2  REFUTED.  For every weight |S_N^phi - zeta| = sqrt(N)|M_phi(s)| + O(N^{-1/2}),
      M_phi(s)=int_0^1 phi(u)u^{-s}du; the ratio |E|sqrt(N) is unbounded (grows like N^{1/2}),
      not bounded.  Max |E|sqrt(N) over N=1e2..1e5: sharp 7070.37, phi1 490.126, phi2 11.7718, phi3 797.298, phiE 2614.23, phiE0 184.817.
